  "status": "candidate record. Conversion flow and page changes: the publication band is removed, Media is badged 'Subscribe for free', the hero doors link to their pages, the offer pages pair with each other, and route changes use the ruled-line transition.",
  "scopeRequested": "Krish, 2026-09-25: \"lets get rid of this section everywhere in this repo [The reading, if you want it separately.], and then add a \\\"Subscribe for free\\\" badge to the Media menu item, and then figure out how we encourage subscriptions on the overall page UX ... the AI GTM and AI Brain buttons in the homepage hero section incorrectly link to the bottom Get my free brief section instead of their respective pages ... the AI Brain enables an AI GTM, and the AI GTM runs better with an AI Brain ... the transitions between pages feel incredibly glitchy and sudden, I want something never seen before but very subtle and classy.\" The plan was approved in session before implementation.",
  "sessionDecisions": [
    "Three intents, three labels: Get your free AI brief (ready), Build your AI brain / Build your AI GTM (exploring), Subscribe for free (not ready). No new label for an existing intent.",
    "The R3 source stays immutable. The doors and Media change as a counted generator transform, the same mechanism the adapter already uses for delivery.",
    "Subscription is offered in three places (menu badge, footer, brief success) and never as a band, pop-up or modal. It stays a hairline action beneath the brief's filled mint.",
    "The LeadBrief's interest checkbox and every lead-delivery boundary are unchanged; the success step only links out.",
    "Page changes: same-origin links stay in the app, the target's code is fetched first, and a view transition sets the new page in behind a mint hairline. Back and Forward are not animated and restore scroll. Reduced motion and unsupported browsers navigate without animation."
  ],
